84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Software development involves continuous code changes that are commonly submitted through Pull Requests for review before integration. Code review plays a critical role in maintaining software quality, security, and reliability, but manual review requires significant developer effort and may overlook subtle defects.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Recent advances in Large Language Models \(LLMs\) have demonstrated their ability to understand and reason about source code. However, automated code review remains challenging because effective review often requires repository-level context, accurate defect identification, and reliable verification of generated findings. Recent research has specifically identified context selection, defect detection, false-alarm reduction, and integration with developer workflows as major challenges in automated code review. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The proposed project develops an Agentic AI Code Reviewer that combines multiple specialized AI agents with static-analysis and dependency-scanning tools. Instead of relying on a single LLM response, the system divides the review into specialized tasks and uses a verification stage to validate potential issues.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Modern software development relies on Pull Requests \(PRs\) and code reviews to identify defects before code is merged into a software project. However, manual code review is time-consuming and may fail to consistently detect security vulnerabilities, logical errors, inadequate error handling, missing tests, and dependency-related risks, particularly in large repositories.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The system will integrate with GitHub Pull Requests, analyze changed code along with relevant repository context, identify potential defects, and generate structured review comments containing the issue, severity, evidence, confidence, and recommended remediation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
