90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (The proposed work aims to improve the efficiency, accuracy, and reliability of automated code review by using an Agentic AI-based approach for GitHub Pull Requests. The system will analyze code changes from multiple perspectives, including security vulnerabilities, logical defects, error handling, testing adequacy, and dependency risks. By combining Large Language Model \(LLM\) reasoning with static-analysis tools such as Semgrep and Bandit, the system can provide both contextual understanding and technical evidence. This reduces the dependency on manual review for identifying common issues and helps developers receive timely feedback before code is merged.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (A key significance of the proposed system is its focus on reducing false positives and improving trust in AI-generated reviews. Instead of accepting every finding generated by an AI model, a dedicated verification agent will validate findings using the changed code, repository context, and analysis-tool results. The system will also incorporate failure handling for large Pull Requests and unsuccessful AI operations. Its performance can be evaluated using real historical software defects through metrics such as precision, recall, F1-score, false-positive rate, detection rate, review time, and cost. Thus, the project provides not only a practical AI-based code-review solution but also a measurable framework for studying the reliability of Agentic AI in software engineering.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
